WEBVTT

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:58.000
<v Tom Okafor>Thanks for coming. The board wants the close faster, and frankly so does the audit committee. Let's be concrete about where the days go.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:02:05.000
<v Tom Okafor>Today UK01 locks the ledger on business day seven. Some months day eight. The board pack goes out on day ten, which the audit committee called out in the 2026 findings. They want locked numbers by day four.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:40.000
<v Priya Raman>Honestly, we lose three days just ticking bank lines against invoices, and that's sixty hours a month across the team. Most lines match exactly one invoice; it's the odd ones that need a human.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:32.000
<v Ana Costa>The bank file shows up around one a.m. If we matched overnight I could start the day on exceptions only. I'd want the list before ten, because the cash call is at ten.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:08:30.000
<v Tom Okafor>The other problem is I don't know a task is late until day five. The checklist is seventy-four lines in a spreadsheet, half of them say "Finance" as the owner.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:20.000
<v Priya Raman>If every task had one named person and a due day, most of the waiting would disappear. People wait because nobody knows it's their turn.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:12:10.000
<v Lukas Brenner>From IT: the bank can send MT940 today. CAMT.053 is possible but Barclays need four weeks' notice. I'd rather not build twice.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:52.000
<v Ana Costa>Watch out for FX. Lots of lines are off by a few pence because of rounding. If those go to exceptions, the report is useless.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:40.000
<v Tom Okafor>Let's not touch the ERP ledger itself, and intercompany terms are out of scope this year. Pilot on UK01 in February, then all EU entities by end of May.

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:45.000
<v Priya Raman>Three days is ambitious. I'd say four for the pilot, three once the automation is stable.

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:30.000
<v Tom Okafor>Board wants three. Let's aim for three by end of June and see where the pilot lands.
